From fd68368e35fda4e9fbe27b02065afc408d74d4c7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kairui Song <kasong@tencent.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 18:16:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 12/17] mm/huge_memory: mark folio as accessed more accurately
 on split

The behavior of updating the folio's access info isn't consistent for
huge mapping splitting or ordinary unmapping. The page table's young
flag has to be translated into folio's access info.

Right now it only check and set folio's referenced flag, which isn't
enough since folio flags update on access have its rules. Ordinary
unmapping (zapping) calls folio_mark_accessed(), and it also checks
if the VMA has recency to avoid false updates.

So first just use the right helper here to be more consistent.

Tested-by: zhaozhengzhuo <zhaozhengzhuo@uniontech.com>
Signed-off-by: Kairui Song <kasong@tencent.com>
Tested-by: syzbot@syzkaller.appspotmail.com
Fixes: 6cbdd9726fb5 ("mm/mglru: use folio_mark_accessed to replace folio_set_active")
Signed-off-by: Barry Song (Xiaomi) <baohua@kernel.org>
